#### User Registration and Login Management

**Files involved:** `main.py` (UserManager class), `register.html`, `login.html`

**Pseudocode:**

```
CLASS UserManager
    FUNCTION register(username, password)
        IF user_exists(username)
            RETURN False
        ENDIF
        user = { "username": username, "password": password }
        append user as JSON line to USERS_FILE
        RETURN True
    END

    FUNCTION login(username, password)
        users = load all users from USERS_FILE (each line JSON decoded)
        FOR each user in users
            IF user.username == username AND user.password == password
                RETURN True
            ENDIF
        ENDFOR
        RETURN False
    END

    FUNCTION user_exists(username)
        users = load all users from USERS_FILE
        FOR each user in users
            IF user.username == username
                RETURN True
            ENDIF
        ENDFOR
        RETURN False
    END

    FUNCTION _load_users()
        IF USERS_FILE does not exist
            RETURN empty list
        ENDIF
        OPEN USERS_FILE for reading
        FOR each line in file
            TRY parse JSON line as user
            ADD user to users list
            EXCEPT JSON error: skip line
        ENDFOR
        RETURN users list
    END

    FUNCTION _save_user(user)
        OPEN USERS_FILE for appending
        WRITE JSON string of user + newline
    END
ENDCLASS

---

HTML Template: register.html
<form method="POST" action="/register">
    Input fields for username and password (required)
    Submit button "Register"
    Display error message if any
    Link to login page
</form>

HTML Template: login.html
<form method="POST" action="/">
    Input fields for username and password (required)
    Submit button "Login"
    Display error message if any
    Link to registration page
</form>
```

**Key functionality:**

- Users can register with unique usernames.
- User credentials are stored as JSON lines in a text file.
- Login verifies credentials against stored users.
- Simple file-based persistence without database.
- Flask routes handle registration and login views with form validation and error messages.

**Third-party library usage:**

- **Flask**: Used for web routing, session management, rendering HTML templates.
- **json**: For serialization/deserialization of user data.
- **os**: For file existence checks.

