['|Case|:login\n\n```plaintext\nCLASS UserManager\n    FUNCTION __init__(users_file)\n        SET self.users_file = users_file\n        SET self.users = load_users()\n\n    FUNCTION login(username, password)\n        RETURN self.users.get(username) == password\n\n    FUNCTION load_users()\n        SET users = {}\n        TRY\n            OPEN self.users_file AS f\n                FOR EACH line IN f\n                    SPLIT line BY \'|\'\n                    SET users[username] = password\n        EXCEPT FileNotFoundError\n            PASS\n        RETURN users\n\nCLASS Main\n    FUNCTION setup_routes()\n        @self.app.route(\'/login\', methods=[\'POST\'])\n        FUNCTION do_login()\n            SET username = request.form[\'username\']\n            SET password = request.form[\'password\']\n            IF self.user_manager.login(username, password)\n                SET session[\'username\'] = username\n                RETURN redirect(\'/dashboard\')\n            RETURN redirect(\'/\')\n```\n\nThird-Party Libraries Used:\n- Flask: A web framework used to create web applications. It provides routing, session management, and request handling.\n\n---\n\n```pseudocode\nFUNCTION login(username: STRING, password: STRING) RETURNS BOOLEAN\n    IF NOT EXISTS USERS_FILE\n        RETURN FALSE\n    ENDIF\n    OPEN USERS_FILE FOR READING\n    FOR EACH line IN file\n        SPLIT line INTO stored_username AND stored_password\n        IF stored_username EQUALS username AND stored_password EQUALS password\n            SET self.username TO username\n            SET self.password TO password\n            RETURN TRUE\n        ENDIF\n    ENDFOR\n    RETURN FALSE\nEND FUNCTION\n```\n\nKey Functionality:\n- The `login` function checks if the provided username and password match any stored credentials, returning true if a match is found.\n\n---\n\n```\nCLASS UserManager\n    FUNCTION register(username, password)\n        IF user_exists(username)\n            RETURN False\n        ENDIF\n        user = { "username": username, "password": password }\n        append user as JSON line to USERS_FILE\n        RETURN True\n    END\n\n    FUNCTION login(username, password)\n        users = load all users from USERS_FILE (each line JSON decoded)\n        FOR each user in users\n            IF user.username == username AND user.password == password\n                RETURN True\n            ENDIF\n        ENDFOR\n        RETURN False\n    END\n\n    FUNCTION user_exists(username)\n        users = load all users from USERS_FILE\n        FOR each user in users\n            IF user.username == username\n                RETURN True\n            ENDIF\n        ENDFOR\n        RETURN False\n    END\n\n    FUNCTION _load_users()\n        IF USERS_FILE does not exist\n            RETURN empty list\n        ENDIF\n        OPEN USERS_FILE for reading\n        FOR each line in file\n            TRY parse JSON line as user\n            ADD user to users list\n            EXCEPT JSON error: skip line\n        ENDFOR\n        RETURN users list\n    END\n\n    FUNCTION _save_user(user)\n        OPEN USERS_FILE for appending\n        WRITE JSON string of user + newline\n    END\nENDCLASS\n\n---\n\nHTML Template: register.html\n<form method="POST" action="/register">\n    Input fields for username and password (required)\n    Submit button "Register"\n    Display error message if any\n    Link to login page\n</form>\n\nHTML Template: login.html\n<form method="POST" action="/">\n    Input fields for username and password (required)\n    Submit button "Login"\n    Display error message if any\n    Link to registration page\n</form>\n```\n\nThird-Party Libraries Used:\n- Flask: Used for web routing, session management, rendering HTML templates.\n- json: For serialization/deserialization of user data.\n- os: For file existence checks.\n\n---\n\n2. |Case|:add_book_to_reading_list\n\n```pseudocode\nFUNCTION add_to_reading_list(book: Book)\n    IF book NOT IN reading_list\n        APPEND book TO reading_list\n        CALL save_reading_list()\n    ENDIF\nEND FUNCTION\n\nFUNCTION save_reading_list()\n    IF reading_list IS NOT EMPTY\n        OPEN READING_LIST_FILE FOR WRITING\n        FOR EACH line IN lines\n            IF line STARTS WITH username\n                CONTINUE\n            ENDIF\n            WRITE line TO READING_LIST_FILE\n        ENDFOR\n        WRITE username AND reading_list TO READING_LIST_FILE\n    ELSE\n        REMOVE user line FROM READING_LIST_FILE\n    ENDIF\nEND FUNCTION\n```\n\nKey Functionality:\n- The `add_to_reading_list` function checks if a book is already in the user\'s reading list before adding it. It then saves the updated reading list to a file.\n\n---\n\n```\nCLASS ReadingListManager\n    FUNCTION add_book(username, book_id)\n        entries = load reading list entries from READING_LIST_FILE\n        FOR each entry in entries\n            IF entry.username == username AND entry.book_id == book_id\n                RETURN False  # already in list\n            ENDIF\n        ENDFOR\n        append {username, book_id} as JSON line to READING_LIST_FILE\n        RETURN True\n    END\n\n    FUNCTION get_reading_list(username)\n        entries = load reading list entries\n        book_ids = []\n        FOR each entry in entries\n            IF entry.username == username\n                ADD entry.book_id to book_ids\n            ENDIF\n        ENDFOR\n        RETURN book_ids\n    END\n\n    FUNCTION remove_book(username, book_id)\n        entries = load reading list entries\n        new_entries = entries excluding those matching username and book_id\n        IF length(new_entries) == length(entries)\n            RETURN False  # no removal\n        ENDIF\n        overwrite READING_LIST_FILE with new_entries as JSON lines\n        RETURN True\n    END\n\n    FUNCTION _load_reading_list()\n        IF READING_LIST_FILE does not exist\n            RETURN empty list\n        ENDIF\n        OPEN READING_LIST_FILE for reading\n        FOR each line\n            TRY parse JSON line as entry\n            ADD entry to entries list\n            EXCEPT JSON error: skip line\n        ENDFOR\n        RETURN entries list\n    END\n\n    FUNCTION _save_reading_list_entry(entry)\n        OPEN READING_LIST_FILE for appending\n        WRITE JSON string of entry + newline\n    END\n\n    FUNCTION _save_all_reading_list(entries)\n        OPEN READING_LIST_FILE for writing (overwrite)\n        FOR each entry in entries\n            WRITE JSON string of entry + newline\n        ENDFOR\n    END\nENDCLASS\n\n---\n\nHTML Template: reading_list.html\nDisplay username\'s reading list header\nLinks to dashboard and logout\nIF message exists, display it\nIF books exist\n    For each book:\n        Display book title as link to details\n        Display author\n        Form with hidden input "remove_id" and button "Remove"\nELSE\n    Display "Your reading list is empty."\nENDIF\n```\n\nThird-Party Libraries Used:\n- Flask: For routing, session management, and rendering templates.\n- json: For reading/writing reading list data.\n- os: For file checks.\n\n---\n\n3. ', '|Case|:book_search\n\n```pseudocode\nFUNCTION search_books(query: STRING) RETURNS LIST OF Book\n    SET query_lower TO LOWERCASE(query)\n    SET results TO EMPTY LIST\n    FOR EACH book IN books\n        IF query_lower IN book.title.lower() OR query_lower IN book.author.lower() OR query_lower IN book.summary.lower() OR query_lower IN book.description.lower()\n            APPEND book TO results\n        ENDIF\n    ENDFOR\n    RETURN results\nEND FUNCTION\n```\n\nKey Functionality:\n- The `search_books` function searches through the list of books for matches based on the title, author, summary, or description, returning a list of matching books.\n\n---\n\n```\nCLASS BookManager\n    FUNCTION search_books(query)\n        query_lower = lowercase(query)\n        books = load all books from BOOKS_FILE (each line JSON decoded)\n        results = empty list\n        FOR each book in books\n            IF query_lower in book.title.lower() OR\n               query_lower in book.author.lower() OR\n               query_lower in book.summary.lower()\n                ADD book to results\n            ENDIF\n        ENDFOR\n        RETURN results\n    END\n\n    FUNCTION _load_books()\n        IF BOOKS_FILE does not exist\n            RETURN empty list\n        ENDIF\n        OPEN BOOKS_FILE for reading\n        FOR each line in file\n            TRY parse JSON line as book\n            ADD book to books list\n            EXCEPT JSON error: skip line\n        ENDFOR\n        RETURN books list\n    END\nENDCLASS\n\n---\n\nHTML Template: dashboard.html\nDisplay welcome message with username\nLink to reading list and logout\nForm with input "query" for search, submit button "Search"\nIF search results exist\n    Display list of books with:\n        - Link to book details page (book title as link)\n        - Author\n        - Summary\nELSE IF query was submitted but no results\n    Display "No results found for <query>"\nENDIF\n```\n\nThird-Party Libraries Used:\n- Flask: For routing and rendering search results.\n- json: For reading book data.\n- os: For file existence checks.\n\n---\n\n4. |Case|:logout\n\n```pseudocode\nFUNCTION logout()\n    REMOVE username FROM session\n    FLASH message "Logged out successfully."\n    REDIRECT TO login page\nEND FUNCTION\n```\n\nKey Functionality:\n- The `logout` function removes the user\'s session and redirects them to the login page, providing feedback about the logout action.\n\n---\n\n```\nROUTE /logout\n    Remove \'username\' from session\n    Redirect to login page (/)\nEND\n\n---\n\nLogin page (login.html) is shown when user is not logged in.\n```\n\nThird-Party Libraries Used:\n- Flask: Core web framework used for routing, session management, rendering HTML templates.\n\n---']
